# While My Guitar Gently Weeps, verse (figure 25.1)
# Sixteen bars, AB-AB'. The bassline descends A G F# F-natural, one note a bar, under the first
# phrase (and, Pollack says, the third); he types it only once. The A after the final double bar
# is the downbeat of the next section, kept as a bar of its own.
key a

